+## engine-87 (provisional): a passed quick read stays passed; the forecast stops an out at its finish (2026-11-18)
+
+On: `READ_WINDOW` and `FORECAST_FINISH` (two flags, one engine step; QB lane; records docs/reviews/2026-11-18-late-cross.md
+and 2026-11-18-forecast-finish.md on claude/exciting-cori-hc8l4u). On develop 63582b08 (engine-84). The number is
+provisional: Integration renumbers it if 85 (Coverage's `FLAT_SINK`) and 86 (Rules' `HALF_KEY`) do not land first.
+
+**What it repairs.** engine-83's never-touched long runs (Defense, via Integration): slant_flat from trips threw H's flat
+at 3.1 s or later, after his reads had run out and the relook or a late key flip put him back on it. The ball was led
+8-10 yd up the sideline onto the flat's extension, and caught 12-16 yd deep with the nearest defender 4-7 yd away. Taught
+slant-flat throws the flat on the plant to its landmark, or not at all.
+
+**READ_WINDOW: on a quick concept a read his eyes have moved off is dead for the play.**
+- The progression advances on its own clock (the dwell and the plan's beats), unchanged.
+- Kept on the read he ends each tick on, so a move that a later reorder (a key flip) or reset undoes within the tick
+  still counts. Neither QB_RELOOK, a reset nor a key flip reopens a dead read.
+- Out of live reads, the plan's checkdown gets one more look, then the best live option, else the existing pocket break
+  or throwaway.
+- Only quick concepts (`concept.family === 'quick'`) are touched.
+
+**FORECAST_FINISH: an out that finishes is forecast to stop at its finish.**
+- Under ROUTE_FINISH an outward route that runs out of field stops at its margin, in bounds. The forecast kept his
+  velocity past it, so the speed out was led 2-3 yd from the sideline instead of to the numbers.
+- On, a route whose last point is its finish ends there in the forecast, as the receiver does. Rules' out-trace with
+  ROUTE_SHAPE: quick-out completions 42 -> 44 of 56, miss on completions 0.91 -> 0.78 yd.
+- The extension-lead part proposed in the late-cross record is not in this landing. Under ROUTE_END a flat past his
+  declared points runs on up the sideline, so a forecast holding him at his landmark would be a false belief that
+  steers the aim. The late flat is a decision, and READ_WINDOW removes it on its own (below). Tried in this landing, the
+  hold also moved three other lanes' fixtures (forecast-break, pursuit-commit, rush-lean-bound), because the defenders'
+  ball estimate shares the forecast. Without it, none move.
+
+**Late-cross probe** (`scripts/diag/eyes/late-cross.ts`, slant_flat from gun_trips_11 × 8 coverages × 3 rosters × 4
+seeds × flip, 176 plays, on this tree):
+
+| arm | throws | late (3.1 s+) and long (1.3 s+ flight) | flats with a 1.3 s+ flight | completions | 20+ yd plays | yards a throw |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| both off (engine-84) | 176 | 49 | 52 | 120 | 36 | 15.5 |
+| READ_WINDOW only | 92 | 0 | 0 | 61 | 2 | 8.1 |
+| FORECAST_FINISH only | 176 | 49 | 52 | 120 | 36 | 15.5 (no finish routes on this concept) |
+| both (engine-87) | 92 | 0 | 0 | 61 | 2 | 8.1 |
+
+With READ_WINDOW the other 84 plays end in a throwaway, a scramble or a sack instead of the late flat.
+
+**Games** (an earlier READ_WINDOW, without the per-tick bookkeeping, on engine-83 fe150600; 8 games, seeds 11 and 31),
+off -> on:
+- completion 0.694 -> 0.694;
+- time to throw p50 2.70 -> 2.70;
+- sacks 4.6% -> 5.8%, throwaways 5.1% -> 6.2%;
+- interceptions 9 -> 14. 4 of the 14 are on quick concepts, the only plays the flag changes; none is on a reopened
+  read. The other 10 are on concepts it does not touch (game divergence).
+
+Integration cards this landing on six seeds.
